\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces \xpg@aux {}{english}\ignorespaces Conceptual flow of the Less-is-Better tokenizer. The Memorizer introduces longer units, which can reduce token count while increasing vocabulary size. The Forgetter removes less useful types, reducing vocabulary size while potentially increasing the number of tokens needed for a text. Their interaction is intended to approach a relatively stable vocabulary. Original schematic based on the mechanism described by \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\textcite {yang2024rethinking}.}}{8}{figure.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tokenizer-lib-model}{{2.1}{8}{\texorpdfstring {\xpg@aux {\xpg@current@opts }{\languagename }}{}\ignorespaces Conceptual flow of the Less-is-Better tokenizer. The Memorizer introduces longer units, which can reduce token count while increasing vocabulary size. The Forgetter removes less useful types, reducing vocabulary size while potentially increasing the number of tokens needed for a text. Their interaction is intended to approach a relatively stable vocabulary. Original schematic based on the mechanism described by \textcite {yang2024rethinking}}{figure.2.1}{}}
